  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "L10_002_Default Values",
   "display_name": "Default Values",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Like any function, <code>__init__</code> can have <b>default values</b> for its parameters. An attribute can also be set to a fixed starting value that is not a parameter at all:</p>\n<pre>class Player:\n    def __init__(self, name, level=1):\n        self.name = name\n        self.level = level\n        self.score = 0        # every player starts with 0\n\np = Player(&quot;Asha&quot;)\nq = Player(&quot;Ravi&quot;, 5)\nprint(p.name, p.level, p.score)\nprint(q.name, q.level, q.score)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>Asha 1 0\nRavi 5 0</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Account</code> whose constructor takes <code>owner</code> and an optional <code>balance</code> (default <code>0</code>), and stores them as attributes <code>owner</code> and <code>balance</code>. Every account also gets an attribute <code>history</code>, starting as an empty list.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>a = Account(\"Asha\")</code>, <code>a.balance</code> is <code>0</code> and <code>a.history</code> is <code>[]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Account:\n    def __init__(self, owner, balance=0):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# a = Account(\"Asha\")\n# print(a.owner, a.balance, a.history)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "a = Account(\"Asha\")\nprint(a.owner, a.balance, a.history)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "Asha 0 []",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "b = Account(\"Ravi\", 500)\nprint(b.owner, b.balance, b.history)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "Ravi 500 []",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "a = Account(\"A\")\nb = Account(\"B\")\na.history.append(1)\nprint(a.history, b.history)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1] []",
