  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L10_003_Objects Are Independent",
   "display_name": "Objects Are Independent",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Each object has <b>its own</b> attributes. Changing an attribute of one object does not affect another object of the same class. Attributes can be changed from outside with the dot: <code>obj.attr = new_value</code>.</p>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">c1 : Counter</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">count = 5</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">c2 : Counter</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">count = 0</div></div></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">c1.count = 5 changed only c1</div>\n<pre>class Counter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.count = 0\n\nc1 = Counter()\nc2 = Counter()\nc1.count = 5\nprint(c1.count, c2.count)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>5 0</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Lamp</code> whose constructor takes <code>room</code> and stores it as the attribute <code>room</code>; every lamp also starts with the attribute <code>on</code> equal to <code>False</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>l = Lamp(\"kitchen\")</code>, <code>l.on</code> is <code>False</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Lamp:\n    def __init__(self, room):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# l = Lamp(\"kitchen\")\n# print(l.room, l.on)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
