  {
   "xml_index": 10,
   "xml_name": "L10_010_A Clock Time",
   "display_name": "A Clock Time",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Here is a class that keeps its attributes within limits: minutes always from 0 to 59, hours from 0 to 23.</p>\n<p><b>Python fact:</b> <code>str(n).zfill(2)</code> gives the number with at least 2 digits: <code>str(5).zfill(2)</code> is <code>\"05\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Time</code> whose constructor takes <code>h</code> and <code>m</code> (valid hours and minutes), with:</p>\n<ul><li><code>__str__</code> returning the time as <code>HH:MM</code> with two digits each (for example <code>09:05</code>);</li><li><code>add_minutes(n)</code> moving the time forward by <code>n</code> minutes (a non-negative integer), wrapping around after <code>23:59</code> to <code>00:00</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, after <code>t = Time(23, 50)</code> and <code>t.add_minutes(15)</code>, <code>print(t)</code> prints <code>00:05</code>.</p>",
