  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L10_013_Counting Objects",
   "display_name": "Counting Objects",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A class attribute can count how many objects have been created: the constructor adds 1 to it each time. Each object can also remember <b>its own</b> number.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Ticket</code> with a class attribute <code>count</code> starting at <code>0</code>. The constructor takes <code>name</code>, stores it, adds 1 to <code>Ticket.count</code>, and gives the ticket an attribute <code>number</code> equal to the new count (so the first ticket is number 1, the second number 2, ...).</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>a = Ticket(\"Asha\")</code> and <code>b = Ticket(\"Ravi\")</code> (the first two tickets), <code>b.number</code> is <code>2</code> and <code>Ticket.count</code> is <code>2</code>.</p>",
