   "xml_index": 17,
   "xml_name": "L10_017_Objects Inside Objects",
   "display_name": "Objects Inside Objects",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>An object's attribute can be a list of <b>other objects</b>. A <code>Library</code> object, for example, can hold <code>Book</code> objects. This is called <b>composition</b>: a big object is built from smaller ones.</p>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">lib : Library</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">books = &#x27;[b1, b2]&#x27;</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;padding:22px 6px 0 0;color:#8a939c\">&rarr;</div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">b1 : Book</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">title = &#x27;Godan&#x27;</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">author = &#x27;Premchand&#x27;</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">b2 : Book</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">title = &#x27;Gitanjali&#x27;</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">author = &#x27;Tagore&#x27;</div></div></div></div>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the class <code>Book</code> is given. Write a class <code>Library</code> whose constructor starts with an empty list <code>books</code>, with methods:</p>\n<ul><li><code>add(book)</code> adds a <code>Book</code> object to the list;</li><li><code>titles_by(author)</code> returns a list of the titles of the books by <code>author</code>, in the order they were added.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, after adding <code>Book(\"Godan\", \"Premchand\")</code> to an empty library <code>lib</code>, <code>lib.titles_by(\"Premchand\")</code> returns <code>['Godan']</code>.</p>",
