   "xml_index": 18,
   "xml_name": "L10_018_Transfer Between Accounts",
   "display_name": "Transfer Between Accounts",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Methods can work on <b>two objects</b> at once: the object the method is called on (<code>self</code>) and another one passed as a parameter.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Account</code> whose constructor takes <code>owner</code> and <code>balance</code>, with the method <code>transfer(other, amount)</code>: if this account's balance is at least <code>amount</code>, move <code>amount</code> from this account to the account <code>other</code> and return <code>True</code>; otherwise change nothing and return <code>False</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>a = Account(\"Asha\", 100)</code> and <code>b = Account(\"Ravi\", 20)</code>, <code>a.transfer(b, 30)</code> returns <code>True</code>, leaving <code>a.balance</code> 70 and <code>b.balance</code> 50.</p>",
