  {
   "xml_index": 24,
   "xml_name": "L10_024_A Fraction Class",
   "display_name": "A Fraction Class",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>To finish, a complete small class. A <b>fraction</b> <code>n/d</code> is stored in <b>lowest terms</b>: numerator and denominator are divided by their greatest common divisor (gcd), and the denominator is kept positive.</p>\n<p><b>Python fact:</b> <code>import math</code> at the top of your code, then <code>math.gcd(a, b)</code> gives the greatest common divisor of two integers (for example <code>math.gcd(6, 8)</code> is 2, and <code>math.gcd(0, 5)</code> is 5).</p>\n<p><code>a/b + c/d = (a*d + c*b) / (b*d)</code> and <code>(a/b) * (c/d) = (a*c) / (b*d)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a class <code>Fraction</code> whose constructor takes integers <code>n</code> and <code>d</code> (<code>d</code> is never 0) and stores them in lowest terms with a positive denominator, as attributes <code>n</code> and <code>d</code>. Methods:</p>\n<ul><li><code>__str__</code> returns <code>n/d</code> (for example <code>3/4</code>), or just <code>n</code> if the denominator is 1;</li><li><code>plus(other)</code> and <code>times(other)</code> return <b>new</b> <code>Fraction</code> objects.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>print(Fraction(1, 2).plus(Fraction(1, 4)))</code> prints <code>3/4</code>, and <code>print(Fraction(6, -8))</code> prints <code>-3/4</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define the class Fraction (import math for math.gcd).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(Fraction(1, 2).plus(Fraction(1, 4)))\n# print(Fraction(6, -8))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
